{"title":"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems\">2003 AMC 12B #15</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems\">2003 AMC 10B #23</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A regular octagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> has an area of one square unit. What is the area of the rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e91fa584790bd73c21e57d1c0bdc5199237b961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ef8af0ec716cfeea89017a030c7d57d3b40e4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(8pt)); pair C=dir(22.5), B=dir(67.5), A=dir(112.5), H=dir(157.5), G=dir(202.5), F=dir(247.5), E=dir(292.5), D=dir(337.5); draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--G--H--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NNW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NNE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,ENE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,ESE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SSE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SSW); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,WSW); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,WNW);[/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"118\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/a/8aa5bd1dc98120acecc2647f8fa765250d3cba81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1-\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt2}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\sqrt2-1\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}2\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"518\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LREcUjK-56U&amp;feature=youtu.be\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LREcUjK-56U&amp;feature=youtu.be</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here is an easy way to look at this, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the perimeter, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Apothem\" title=\"Apothem\">apothem</a>:\n</p><p>Area of Octagon: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de131f1f0a0d551897d178eccf881254a908729a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ap}{2}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>Area of Rectangle: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccaa941dcbae69d1493febaac370adf0ceeb1b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{8}\\times 2a=\\dfrac{2ap}{8}=\\frac{ap}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>You can see from this that the octagon's area is twice as large as the rectangle's area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1521e0827b3737d6bd56920ff13324b3b97f8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a9e9c63ae7f93d28c6a8e83ab8b76c83a6f147.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(8pt)); pair C=dir(22.5), B=dir(67.5), A=dir(112.5), H=dir(157.5), G=dir(202.5), F=dir(247.5), E=dir(292.5), D=dir(337.5); draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--G--H--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NNW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NNE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,ENE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,ESE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SSE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SSW); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,WSW); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,WNW);  draw(A--E--F--B--C--G--H--D); draw(A--E--F--B--A,blue); draw(A--F--E--B--A,red); [/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"118\" />\n</p><p>Here is a less complicated way than that of the user below. If you draw a line segment from each vertex to the center of the octagon and draw the rectangle ABEF (in red), you can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the triangles (in blue) share the same base and height with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4a7df1100efe353cc612d5d1c289c22d5bf8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> the rectangle. Therefore, the rectangle's area is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638ee7316e2377ea24df5d33afe4ead7a45fee2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles, and is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1521e0827b3737d6bd56920ff13324b3b97f8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" /> the area of the octagon.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a83fa1ab65b5ad398b3743d61186fe7a87c34209.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(8pt)); pair C=dir(22.5), B=dir(67.5), A=dir(112.5), H=dir(157.5), G=dir(202.5), F=dir(247.5), E=dir(292.5), D=dir(337.5); draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--G--H--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NNW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NNE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,ENE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,ESE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SSE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SSW); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,WSW); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,WNW);  draw(A--D--E--H--G--B--C--F); [/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"118\" />\nDrawing lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f2ef2fa9310285ea0bc63937e3bf83c99168a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90b19c0bfdec36082e8da6e7ba3a3149b69fa63c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />, we can see that the octagon is comprised of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rectangles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles. The triangles each are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22231a5cdd4fe05a11f4b577e3b81221f3017a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> triangles, and since their diagonal is length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, each of their sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97a62890d87757ecbbfa2c66894efdc16ca4f8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"40\" height=\"43\" />. The area of the entire figure is, likewise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> (the square)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fc2587d106d60603b58c61aed8888075e7440ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+4x^2\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"67\" height=\"41\" /> (the 4 rectangles)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d8c5d514ad292dc3e1dfb94e40ea9b67f6273a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+2\\cdot(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"41\" /> (the triangles), which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac433b651c82a32c4acf5bfe11bcc89cd32eba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2 + 2\\sqrt{2}x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e91fa584790bd73c21e57d1c0bdc5199237b961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb69cd00d15ce0ee6aa93b9072e7db7e76c8faf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x+\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"41\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/1/e71ff3655ae7479788de14fa5050165b4204ce28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />, which we can see is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc40b39fdfc16c2f7849255417487c046bb9399b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ABCDEFGH}{2} =  \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"205\" height=\"48\" /> the area of the octagon.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we are going to divide the diagram. Now we need to find the ratio of the area of the rectangle to the area of the trapezoid. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c153839e87140be8666011f784d5c1564b31f2d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(8pt)); pair C=dir(22.5), B=dir(67.5), A=dir(112.5), H=dir(157.5), G=dir(202.5), F=dir(247.5), E=dir(292.5), D=dir(337.5); draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--G--H--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NNW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NNE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,ENE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,ESE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SSE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SSW); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,WSW); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,WNW);draw(A--F);draw(B--E);draw(D--G);draw(C--H);[/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"118\" />\n</p><p>The area of a trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/993ba573c8add83425365bc66f1544732ae7073e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b_1 + b_2}{2}h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"37\" />\nNote that the trapezoid is made out of 2 45-45-90 triangles and a rectangle, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff7577f4acd036e4f48bed742c91c9b1416c795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH=FG=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />. By realizing that, the area of the trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa88cab81d7774d69631053f496bedaca564331f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{2})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"43\" />). To make this product easier, note there is two trapezoids, so the new product is now this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d994094c9f138ee1438ff91c27309e3101b0743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{2})(\\sqrt{2}) = \\sqrt{2} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"194\" height=\"43\" /> \n</p><p>Notice how the rectangle has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc749b0e7d47fb1f19fa539c653c3cdf3a15bd2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so it's area is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc749b0e7d47fb1f19fa539c653c3cdf3a15bd2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The ratio of the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e91fa584790bd73c21e57d1c0bdc5199237b961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> to the two trapezoids is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c24ac2a2a3d8ab9f3f0f63c567f2a56164c670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, meaning they share half the area of the octagon. Since the area of the octagon is 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a63588d48cc9015ddcfc1560cf86e98b33b51972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\therefore$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> the area of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1521e0827b3737d6bd56920ff13324b3b97f8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~ghfhgvghj10\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B\">2003 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"20